                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ecc2cdf-2a9e-3113-88e2-b4e8ca071662",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6e4488-a249-38aa-9b83-2413abf2f046",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To reduce to a residue of ash. See ashing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1dccb8de-78bb-4688-82b5-b5351e1707ce",
                                                "sense_id": "6ecc2cdf-2a9e-3113-88e2-b4e8ca071662",
                                                "text": "I dried the extracted leather very slowly on the steam bath […] until the substance was dry enough to ash. […] I think that the discrepancy in the percentages of \"total ash\" by method No. 2 and No. 6 is due to this excessive heat required to ash the leather […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6e5e02e-462d-44d9-9907-6cb90fcd311f",
                                                "sense_id": "6ecc2cdf-2a9e-3113-88e2-b4e8ca071662",
                                                "text": "The inorganic material left after ashing lung tissue specimens not only contains inhaled particles but also very large quantities of inorganic residue derived from the tissue itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "216cfd87-e178-40cf-a4bd-6ee3a5f5b1cf",
                                                "sense_id": "6ecc2cdf-2a9e-3113-88e2-b4e8ca071662",
                                                "text": "Ash and silica contents of the plant material were determined by classical gravimetric techniques. Tissue samples were ashed in platinum crucibles at about 500 °C, and the ash was treated repeatedly with 6 N hydrochloric acid to remove other mineral impurities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91597dad-f7a7-4c1f-a3e6-2f51bc708e29",
                                                "sense_id": "6ecc2cdf-2a9e-3113-88e2-b4e8ca071662",
                                                "text": "A 10-g food sample was dried, then ashed, and analyzed for salt (NaCl) content by the Mohr titration method (AgNO₃ + Cl → AgCl). The weight of the dried sample was 2g, and the ashed sample weight was 0.5g."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b23d4419-a115-3d30-acc5-fd7cd4ec184b",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6e4488-a249-38aa-9b83-2413abf2f046",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hit the end off (a burning cigar or cigarette)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f614816-b0cb-45fd-a5a2-26d24e6adbeb",
                                                "sense_id": "b23d4419-a115-3d30-acc5-fd7cd4ec184b",
                                                "text": "\"Nonsense,\" Mrs. Gardiner challenged, ashing her cigarette."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f76f63b7-dedd-4396-b819-1b8f4580b444",
                                                "sense_id": "b23d4419-a115-3d30-acc5-fd7cd4ec184b",
                                                "text": "He realized that he was standing staring at her and he sat down quickly, making a business of ashing his cigarette."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5544d1a-6021-4a3a-9e67-3296193afadf",
                                                "sense_id": "b23d4419-a115-3d30-acc5-fd7cd4ec184b",
                                                "text": "Hamilton ashed his cigar, and studied the end of it for some moments without speaking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d597718-5b74-4fb9-821b-e4a4c44333f3",
                                                "sense_id": "b23d4419-a115-3d30-acc5-fd7cd4ec184b",
                                                "text": "‘He’s right, you know,’ said Archie earnestly, ashing a fag in an empty curry bowl."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7900415e-072b-38b9-81dd-a00646e66313",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6e4488-a249-38aa-9b83-2413abf2f046",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mark (someone) with an ashen cross on the forehead to observe Ash Wednesday."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a70b746b-9fde-3caa-b104-5621c61f3bc3",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6e4488-a249-38aa-9b83-2413abf2f046",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover newly-sown fields of crops with ashes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38e36d6a-4843-48cb-9fe2-359bc551056d",
                                                "sense_id": "a70b746b-9fde-3caa-b104-5621c61f3bc3",
                                                "text": "Last spring, after I planted, I took what ashes I have saved during the last year, and put on my corn […] . On harvesting I cut up the two rows which were not ashed (or twenty rods of them,) and set them apart from the others in stouts; and then I cut up two rows of the same length, on each side, which had been ashed, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "903b00da-cd45-41b6-bf7f-9356e25ee641",
                                                "sense_id": "a70b746b-9fde-3caa-b104-5621c61f3bc3",
                                                "text": "After the corn was planted, upon acre A, I spread broadcast one hundred bushels of lime, (cost $3) and fifty bushels of ashes, (cost $6.) […] The extra crop of the combination over the limed acre or ashed, was paid by the increased crop, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
